avformat/mpegtsenc: carry SCTE-35 as a section stream

Rebased onto FFmpeg 8.0; applies cleanly to release/8.1, release/9.0 and master.
Upstream took the demuxer half (mpegts.c recognises stream_type 0x86 behind a CUEI
registration descriptor) but the muxer still has nothing, so an SCTE-35 stream leaves
as private data and no packager sees it. Proposed upstream in Nov 2021, Jul 2023 and
Jun 2025, unmerged each time.

Three changes:

  1. get_dvb_stream_type(): AV_CODEC_ID_SCTE_35 -> stream_type 0x86.
  2. mpegts_write_pmt(): emit the CUEI registration descriptor at program level when the
     service carries a cue stream, as ANSI/SCTE 35 requires. Without it even FFmpeg's own
     demuxer ignores the 0x86 stream. The stream-membership test is factored into
     service_has_stream() so the new pre-pass and the existing loop agree.
  3. mpegts_write_packet_internal(): write the splice_info_section as PSI rather than PES.

Known limitation: -max_delay shifts the media's PES timestamps but cannot shift a
splice_time without rewriting the section, so cues drift against media if it is set.
It defaults to 0 and ingestlab never sets it.

